Leave the symbol version script out on zedBSD.

libxkbcommon links its library with a version script whenever the linker
accepts one, which gives every exported symbol a version.  zedBSD's
loader does not read symbol versions and its libraries carry none (the
package contract checks for that), so on zedBSD the script is not used.
Other systems are unchanged.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -308,7 +308,8 @@
 
 # Supports -Wl,--version-script?
 meson_test_map = meson.current_source_dir() / 'test/meson_test.map'
-have_version_script = cc.links(
+# zedBSD's loader does not read symbol versions, so its libraries carry none.
+have_version_script = host_machine.system() != 'zedbsd' and cc.links(
     'int main(void) { return 0; }',
     args: f'-Wl,--version-script=@meson_test_map@',
     name: '-Wl,--version-script',
